# Booking workflow — agent reference

This rule is the single source of truth for the **new booking lifecycle** described in `docs/archive/planning/NEW_FLOW_PLAN.md` (plan) and `docs/archive/planning/NEW_FLOW.md` (original spec).

Whenever a task touches **booking state, emails, PDF persistence, or the admin dashboard**, start here.

## 1. Status enum (canonical)

Use the string literals below in DB, code, and UI. **Postgres storage:** `TEXT` + `CHECK (status IN (...))` — see `docs/archive/planning/NEW_FLOW_PLAN.md` §6.1 **Q1.3** (avoid Postgres `ENUM` churn). Keep a single source (`supabase/functions/_shared/statusMachine.ts` on the server, `ui/src/features/dashboard/bookings/lib/workflow.ts` on the client — keep in sync).

```
PENDING_REVIEW
PENDING_DOCUMENTS
PENDING_GAF
PENDING_PARKING_REQUEST
PENDING_PET_REQUEST
READY_FOR_CHECKIN
READY_FOR_CHECKOUT
PENDING_SD_REFUND
COMPLETED
CANCELLED
IMPORTED
```

> **`IMPORTED`** — reached only by **`import-commit`** direct insert for **past** check-ins (before today, Asia/Manila). **Today/future** imported rows commit as **`PENDING_REVIEW`** with **`imported_from_batch_id`** set (UI shows Pending Review; **Imported** status filter still finds them when explicitly selected). Not via `workflowOrchestrator.transition()`. Manual overrides: **`IMPORTED → CANCELLED`** (import revert) or **`IMPORTED → PENDING_REVIEW`** (pull a past import into the live pipeline). Not in `TERMINAL_STATUSES`.

> Legacy DB rows have `status = 'booked'` (or `'canceled'`). The migration maps them per **`docs/archive/planning/NEW_FLOW_PLAN.md` §6.1 Q1.1**: check-in **before today (Asia/Manila)** → `COMPLETED`; check-in **today or future** → `PENDING_REVIEW`; canceled rows → `CANCELLED`.

## 2. Allowed transitions

### 2.1 Primary workflow (happy path + cancel)

```
PENDING_REVIEW              → PENDING_DOCUMENTS | CANCELLED
PENDING_DOCUMENTS           → PENDING_DOCUMENTS | READY_FOR_CHECKIN | CANCELLED
PENDING_GAF                 → PENDING_DOCUMENTS | READY_FOR_CHECKIN | CANCELLED
PENDING_PARKING_REQUEST     → PENDING_DOCUMENTS | READY_FOR_CHECKIN | CANCELLED
PENDING_PET_REQUEST         → PENDING_DOCUMENTS | READY_FOR_CHECKIN | CANCELLED
READY_FOR_CHECKIN           → READY_FOR_CHECKOUT | CANCELLED
READY_FOR_CHECKOUT          → PENDING_SD_REFUND | COMPLETED | CANCELLED
PENDING_SD_REFUND           → COMPLETED | CANCELLED
COMPLETED                   → (terminal)
CANCELLED                   → (terminal)
IMPORTED                    → (no automatic progression — import-insert only)
```

**Manual override from `IMPORTED`:**

```
IMPORTED                    → CANCELLED | PENDING_REVIEW   # admin-only; CANCELLED for import-revert
```

### 2.2 Admin-only exceptional transitions

These exist so humans can recover when automation lags, guest data changes late, or the admin needs to step the booking back one stage to redo a step.

**Forward-only override** (force-advance, e.g. when the Gmail listener / cron is skipped):

```
PENDING_GAF             → READY_FOR_CHECKIN   # approved GAF uploaded manually, no parking/pet sub-stages
READY_FOR_CHECKIN       → PENDING_SD_REFUND   # skip guest SD form stage (manual); no SD form email on this edge
```

**Backward overrides** (one-step-back recovery — the WorkflowPanel surfaces these as a "Back to …" button):

```
PENDING_DOCUMENTS           → PENDING_REVIEW
PENDING_GAF                 → PENDING_DOCUMENTS | PENDING_REVIEW
PENDING_PARKING_REQUEST     → PENDING_DOCUMENTS | PENDING_REVIEW
PENDING_PET_REQUEST         → PENDING_DOCUMENTS | PENDING_REVIEW
READY_FOR_CHECKIN           → PENDING_DOCUMENTS | PENDING_PET_REQUEST | PENDING_PARKING_REQUEST | PENDING_GAF | PENDING_REVIEW | PENDING_SD_REFUND
READY_FOR_CHECKOUT          → READY_FOR_CHECKIN
PENDING_SD_REFUND           → READY_FOR_CHECKOUT
```

The override **graph** is permissive — it lists every back-step that is structurally valid. The **UI** narrows it down via `bookingPipeline()` to a single "Back to …" button that always points at the booking's _immediately previous_ applicable step (e.g. parking is skipped when `need_parking = false`).

**Email safety:** backward transitions never fire outbound email. The orchestrator sends the ready-for-check-in email only on **forward** moves to `READY_FOR_CHECKIN` from `PENDING_REVIEW` (D2 empty-requirements skip), `PENDING_DOCUMENTS` (parent docs complete), or legacy `PENDING_GAF` / `PENDING_PARKING_REQUEST` / `PENDING_PET_REQUEST` — not from e.g. `PENDING_SD_REFUND` → `READY_FOR_CHECKIN`. The **SD refund form request** email is gated on `fromStatus === READY_FOR_CHECKIN && toStatus === READY_FOR_CHECKOUT`, so stepping back from `READY_FOR_CHECKOUT` to `READY_FOR_CHECKIN` does not re-send; admins can re-send from **Automation Triggers** while the booking stays on `READY_FOR_CHECKOUT`.

**SD refund skip (security_deposit=0):** When `security_deposit` is 0 (typical for Airbnb bookings where DP/SD default to 0), the `PENDING_SD_REFUND` step is skipped entirely — `READY_FOR_CHECKOUT` goes directly to `COMPLETED`. The SD refund form request email is not sent, the guest does not see the `/sd-form`, and `sd-refund-cron` suppresses the check-out email for SD=0 bookings. The UI pipeline (`bookingPipeline`) hides `PENDING_SD_REFUND` when `security_deposit === 0`.

**Airbnb source behavior:** Airbnb bookings (`booking_source === 'Airbnb'`, set via `?source=airbnb` on the guest form or admin **Booking Source** edit) differ from Facebook bookings: (1) guest form skips the Payment step (4 steps instead of 5), `paymentReceipt` is not required; (2) `ReviewPricingForm` defaults DP and SD to **₱0** (editable by admin if needed); (3) admin `BookingEditForm` hides the Downpayment receipt document row; (4) `ready-for-checkin` email hides the Payment breakdown + GCash QR section when total balance due is 0 (source-agnostic — applies to any booking with zero total balance); (5) `submit-form` skips downpayment receipt AI validation for Airbnb; (6) **guest balance settlement** excludes booking rate, down payment, and security deposit from total guest balance — only pet fee + additional guest fee count; receipt AI applies only when that fee total is **> ₱0**. Switching source to Airbnb in admin edit zeros DP/SD and clears stale guest balance settlement fields.

**Manual "force advance"** (workflow panel): admins must be able to trigger transitions that would normally be fired by **cron** or the **Gmail listener** when those automations are late or skipped.

Implementation rule: keep **two layers** in `statusMachine.ts`:

1. `canTransition(from, to)` — strict graph for automation + normal admin clicks.
2. `canManualForceTransition(from, to, ctx)` — **small explicit allow-list** of extra edges (e.g. `READY_FOR_CHECKIN → PENDING_SD_REFUND` even before cron, `PENDING_GAF → READY_FOR_CHECKIN` when the approved PDF was uploaded manually, etc.). **Never** accept arbitrary `{ toStatus }` from the client without this second check.

`transition-booking` always calls the orchestrator with `{ manual: true | false }` so the server can tell which validator ran.

The server **must** validate every transition before writing. **Manual advances** and **cron/listener** calls must all go through `workflowOrchestrator.transition()` — never duplicate side-effect logic in callers.

### 2.3 Guest-field edit → revert to review

Only revert `status` back to `PENDING_REVIEW` when both are true:

1. The update came from one of these flows:
   - Public guest update (`/form?bookingId=...`)
   - Admin booking-detail save (`/bookings/:bookingId` edit form → `POST update-booking-details`)
   - Admin guest-document replacement (`upload-booking-asset` for `payment_receipt` | `valid_id` | `pet_vaccination` | `pet_image` only — other asset types do not revert)
2. At least one workflow-sensitive field changed:
   - Facebook / Airbnb Name
   - Primary Guest name
   - Email
   - Phone Number
   - Additional Guest Names
   - Check-in and Check-out Date
   - Check-in and Check-out Time
   - Parking Details
   - Surprise decor request (`guest_requests_surprise_decor`)
   - Pet Details — only sensitive when the property's resolved document requirements include a `has_pets`-triggered requirement or id `pet` (§4.5)
   - Downpayment receipt
   - Valid ID
   - Pet vaccination and pet photo

If only non-listed fields are updated, keep the current status (do **not** revert).

When a listed field changes while the booking’s `status` is one of **`PENDING_DOCUMENTS`**, **`PENDING_GAF`**, **`PENDING_PARKING_REQUEST`**, **`PENDING_PET_REQUEST`**, or **`READY_FOR_CHECKIN`**, set `status` to `PENDING_REVIEW` (and update `status_updated_at`). In the **same write**, apply **`statusMachine.ts#pendingDocumentsClearPatchForGuestEditRevert`**: nested completion timestamps, **approved** PDF URLs, **admin parking settlement** columns, and **guest balance settlement** columns — **not** pricing snapshot fields (`booking_rate`, `down_payment`, `balance`, `security_deposit`, `pet_fee`, `parking_rate_guest`, `guest_additional_fee`) and **not** request PDF URLs (`gaf_request_pdf_url`, `pet_request_pdf_url`) unless PDF fill content changed (`requestPdfClearPatchForChangedFormFields` / admin mirror `requestPdfClearPatchForAdminGuestEdit`). Guest doc uploads (`valid_id`, `pet_vaccination`, `pet_image`) revert status but **preserve** stored request PDFs. **`workflowOrchestrator.ts`** merges the **same patch** at the start of **`PENDING_REVIEW → PENDING_DOCUMENTS | PENDING_GAF`** before payload pricing, preventing stale `*_completed_at` from showing substeps as complete immediately after **Proceed to Pending Documents** without wiping stored pricing unless the payload supplies new values. Proceed then **regenerates** request PDFs when `generatePdf` is on, reusing the prior URL when generation fails, and **throws** if a required request PDF is still missing after proceed. Do **not** apply this revert when status is already **`PENDING_REVIEW`**, in **`READY_FOR_CHECKOUT`** / **`PENDING_SD_REFUND`**, **`COMPLETED`**, or **`CANCELLED`**. Server helper: `statusMachine.ts#shouldRevertGuestFieldEditsToPendingReview`.

**Dev-control checkboxes** on the guest form (save DB, storage, email) still apply to **every** submit/save — reverting status never bypasses them. **PDF generation** is not part of guest submit; it runs from the orchestrator on `PENDING_REVIEW` → initial documents when property automations and resolved requirements allow.

## 3. Side-effect matrix

Each transition fans out a known set of side effects. Implement them inside `_shared/workflowOrchestrator.ts` and call it from the `transition-booking` edge function.

**Plan-tier gating (added 2026-08-24, [`tier-feature-alignment-audit.md`](../../docs/workflow/in-progress/tier-feature-alignment-audit.md) Phase 5):** the transition **graph is identical on every tier** — only the automated **email** side effects are gated, via the `automatedBookingFlow` plan feature. `_shared/propertyAutomationToggles.ts#PLAN_GATED_AUTOMATION_TOGGLE_KEYS` (`emailGafRequest`, `emailBookingAcknowledgement`, `emailPetRequest`, `emailReadyForCheckin`, `emailSdRefundCheckout`) are forced off for a property without the feature, regardless of the property's own saved toggle. **`emailNewBookingRequest`** (the "a guest submitted a form" ops alert) is deliberately **not** plan-gated — it stays free on every tier, same rationale as web chat staying free (core booking loop). **PDF generation is never gated** — the orchestrator throws if a required request PDF is missing after proceed, so treating it as a paid convenience would break the transition itself on Free tier, not just skip a nicety.

When the plan blocks one of these emails, `WorkflowOrchestrator.transition()`'s return adds the skipped side-effect name(s) to `sideEffects.automationSkippedByPlan` (e.g. `'gaf_request'`) — never a silent no-op. Skips because the **host turned the property toggle off** (not plan-blocked) go in `sideEffects.automationSkippedByHost` with a settings-focused toast (no Upgrade CTA). `transition-booking`'s admin caller (`useTransitionBooking.ts`) surfaces plan skips as a toast with an Upgrade CTA and stores a session hint so **Automation Triggers** expands on the booking rail. Scoped **Run check-out move** (`sd-refund-cron` with `{ bookingId }`) on Free: same plan-skip toast when email is suppressed after a successful status move. **Manual send:** `send-booking-workflow-email` (`POST { bookingId, kind }` where `kind` is one of `gaf_request` | `pet_request` | `booking_acknowledgement` | `ready_for_checkin` | `sd_refund_form_request`) uses `rawPropertyAutomationEnabled` (property toggle only — **not** plan-gated). Legacy alias `send-sd-refund-form-email` remains. **`parking-broadcast-email` is retired (410).** Automation Triggers lists eligible Send buttons by status (PDF present, pets, RFCI/RFCO). **Free-tier resend cooldown (1 hour):** after a successful manual send, further sends of the same `kind` are rejected with **429** until the cooldown elapses (`guest_submissions.workflow_email_manual_sent_at`); UI shows **Resend** disabled with a wait tooltip. Paid (`automatedBookingFlow`) has no cooldown. **Property parking** uses **Find parking** / marketplace `linkStay` — not broadcast emails.

**Manual vs. automatic — which check to use:** `propertyAutomationEnabled()`/`resolvePropertyAutomationToggles()` (plan-gated) is for anything the _orchestrator_ or a _scheduled cron_ fires automatically (including `sd-refund-cron`'s admin-scoped "run now," since that re-invokes the same automation, just on demand). `rawPropertyAutomationEnabled()` (property setting only, no plan gate) is for a genuinely distinct manual action a host explicitly clicks specifically because the automated path is blocked or failed — never gate the escape hatch behind the same entitlement it's standing in for. On Free, **Run check-out automation** may still skip the SD email (plan-gated); **Resend / Send Check-out Instructions** is the true email escape hatch.

