## 6. Invariants (tests should cover these)

- `submit-form` never calls Azure GAF `sendEmail`, `sendPetEmail`, or **`generatePDF`** / **`generatePetPDF`** (no guest-submit PDFs). After a successful **DB** save, when the **`sendEmail` query param is not `false`**, it calls **`sendNewBookingRequestNotify`** (owner/ops alert to **`EMAIL_REPLY_TO` only** via `new-booking-request.html`) — not workflow acknowledgement / GAF / pet / parking.
- Only `workflowOrchestrator.transition()` mutates `status` and `status_updated_at` for **workflow transitions** (admin/cron/listener). Status writes use `DatabaseService.updateBookingStatus(..., expectedFrom)` so a concurrent host Proceed is a no-op and the handler returns **409** (`Booking status changed. Refresh and try again.`). **Exception — pipeline / `READY_FOR_CHECKIN` → `PENDING_REVIEW` safety revert** (no orchestrator): `submit-form` when workflow-sensitive guest fields change while `shouldRevertGuestFieldEditsToPendingReview(status)`, admin `POST update-booking-details` from `BookingEditForm` under the same rule (compare-and-swap on current status), and `upload-booking-asset` for guest doc `assetType`s `payment_receipt` | `valid_id` | `pet_vaccination` | `pet_image`. These paths set `status`, `status_updated_at`, and **`pendingDocumentsClearPatchForGuestEditRevert()`** fields in one row update; they do not send workflow emails or call the orchestrator.
- **Exception — admin Reschedule** (`ui/.../hooks/useRescheduleBooking.ts`, booking-detail `⋯` → **Reschedule**, `RescheduleBookingModal`): a host-confirmed date change that also, **mandatorily**, forces `status` → **`PENDING_REVIEW`** (always, so the host re-runs the pricing + document proceed from the top of the pipeline after a date move). Offered only while `canRescheduleBookingAtStatus(status)` (any status before `READY_FOR_CHECKOUT`). One `POST update-booking-details` write: new `check_in_date` / `check_out_date` / `number_of_nights` + `status` + `status_updated_at` + `pendingDocumentsClearPatchForGuestEditRevert()` + `pendingDocumentsClearCompletionsJsonbPatch()`. **No orchestrator, no workflow emails, and request PDFs (`gaf_request_pdf_url` / `pet_request_pdf_url`) are neither cleared nor regenerated** — the host re-sends GAF/pet requests + acknowledgement from **Automation Triggers** if the new dates need fresh paperwork.
- **AI document verdicts are advisory.** An AI `invalid` verdict on a required receipt/document blocks the admin transition by default with a **409 coded `ai_verdict_blocked`** (`_shared/aiVerdictOverride.ts#assertAiVerdictAllowsProceed`, called from `workflowOrchestrator.ts`). A person (`org_owner`, `team_member`, `super_admin`) may resend with **`override_ai_verdict: true`**; the booking detail UI offers **Proceed anyway** (`features/dashboard/bookings/lib/aiVerdictOverride.ts`). Crons, webhooks and the AI assistant can never override. An applied override is recorded as `aiVerdictOverridden: true` in the transition's `activity_log` metadata.
- `get-booked-dates` returns everything where `status <> 'CANCELLED'` (not just `'booked'`).
- **Calendar sync (`calendarSync`, Pro+):** OTA-synced unavailability lands as `property_blocked_dates` rows with **`source='ical_import'`** (`feed_id`/`external_uid` set). Availability + overlap checks (`loadBlockedRanges`, `hasBlockedNightsInRange`, `get-booked-dates`) already return **all** sources, so imported blocks prevent double-booking with no per-caller change. `unblock_property_blocked_dates`'s third arg `p_source_filter` defaults to `'manual'` — the manual unblock path never deletes synced rows; only `calendar-sync-cron` (feed no longer lists the date) or feed removal clears them. **Phase 2 (shipped):** when a feed sets `create_bookings = true`, reservation events are promoted to `guest_submissions` rows carrying `external_source`/`external_uid`/`external_feed_id`/`external_raw`, `booking_source='Airbnb'`, created in **`PENDING_REVIEW`** and **never auto-advanced** by the sync engine (it only creates, guarded-reverts on reschedule, or `transition(...,'CANCELLED')` — the last skipped when the stay is already past check-in, logged `past_checkin_feed_drop`). `workflowOrchestrator.ts#transition` and `sd-refund-cron` **suppress every guest-facing side effect** (acknowledgement / ready-for-check-in / SD-refund-form emails, stay-guide token) while **`guest_email` is blank** — `sideEffects.externalSuppressed` records it. The host forwards `<origin>/form?complete=<token>&property=<slug>` (`issue-guest-form-completion-token` → `get-form-completion` → `submit-form-completion`); that flow UPDATEs the existing row with the guest's details, keeps the stored dates + `booking_source`/`external_*`, leaves `status` at `PENDING_REVIEW`, and stamps `guest_form_completed_at`. Once `guest_email` is populated the normal emails resume on the next admin transition.
- Inbound approval emails are processed **at most once** (idempotency via `processed_emails` keyed on Resend `email_id`).
- Guest SD refund submissions use **`submit-sd-form`** → `WorkflowOrchestrator.transition()` (same invariants as admin transitions); **`get-sd-form`** is read-only and returns **404** unless status is `READY_FOR_CHECKOUT` **or** `READY_FOR_CHECKIN` with `sd_refund_form_emailed_at` set (returns `awaiting_balance_settlement` until status advances).

## 7. Don'ts

- Don't re-introduce `?testing=true` or a separate test-booking pipeline in UI or edge code (use staging/local Supabase instead).
- After the migration ships, **application code** should treat `status` as the **new canonical literals only**. The migration itself may still read legacy `'booked'` / `'canceled'` — that's OK, but delete dead branches once backfill is done.
- Don't put email calls inside `DatabaseService`; keep services single-responsibility.
- Don't add side effects inline to transition endpoints — go through the orchestrator so every caller (UI, Gmail listener, cron) behaves identically.
- Don't forget to update `docs/PROJECT.md` and `docs/todos/` (GitHub Issues + epic specs) per `documentation-maintenance.mdc`.

